Implementation Plan - WeBox Tier 1 & Tier 2 Feature Completion
This plan outlines the complete implementation for missing PRD Tier 1 (Core) and Tier 2 (Advanced) requirements, providing a full-stack, enterprise-grade, English-only meal ordering platform for employees and administrators.

User Review Required
IMPORTANT

Data Consistency & Seed Update: We will preserve existing seeded admin account (admin@webox.com / Admin123) and menu items, and enrich custom options for demo dishes (e.g. burgers, pastas, salads).
Authentication Flow: Replace temporary browser prompt() with a full responsive Auth Modal with persistent sessions (LocalStorage + GET /api/me), role-based routing (Console view for Admins, Employee view for Employees), and clear error messages.
Console Management Architecture: Implement a single-page view switcher in the SPA so administrators can seamlessly toggle between the Employee Menu view and the Console Management dashboard without needing an external routing framework.
Proposed Changes
Backend Components
[MODIFY] 
Repositories.java
Add query methods for checking active orders for a user on a given date and slot.
Add repository helper methods for DailyMenu management by date and dish id.
[MODIFY] 
Api.java
User Session & Preferences:
GET /api/me: Returns current user info (email, role, allergens, preferredCategories, spice, budgetMin, budgetMax).
PUT /api/me/preferences: Updates employee's allergens, preferred categories, spice level, and budget bounds.
Ordering Enhancements:
GET /api/orders/check: Checks if an active order (Pending or Confirmed) already exists for current user for target date + slot.
Enrich order placement logic to ensure full option snapshotting.
Admin Console APIs (Secured with role check: ADMIN only):
GET /api/admin/dishes: List all dishes (both active and inactive).
POST /api/admin/dishes: Create new dish with full metadata (name, description, price, category, protein, spice, allergens, image, optionsJson).
PUT /api/admin/dishes/{id}: Update existing dish details.
PATCH /api/admin/dishes/{id}/status: Toggle active / inactive status.
GET /api/admin/menu?date=YYYY-MM-DD: Get menu schedules and stock for a specified date.
POST /api/admin/menu: Schedule daily menu items and supply stock count for a specified date.
